Package: os7-server
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: metapackages
Priority: important
Depends: os7-base (= @OS7_VERSION@), os7-backup (= @OS7_VERSION@)
Conflicts: os7-desktop
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: OS/7 — the headless product
 What a machine installed in headless mode is. On arm64 it is the only product
 there is: Microsoft ships no arm64 desktop stack, so that architecture is
 server-only and permanently so.
 .
 Conflicts with os7-desktop, because the two are the setup-time choice and not a
 runtime toggle. A machine holding both would be one whose mode nobody chose.
